 "text": "I was reading in the park when the pages started to glow. And the book opened a door. It took me ten years into my future. There I was the car in the house, the life I had only ever dreamed about. But I had one question, how did I get here? The book showed me chapter by chapter. It started on one ordinary night. He wrote his dream down, it looked impossible. He wrote it anyway, that page was a starting point. After that, every single day gave him a choice. He could sleep in. Or get up and give his dream one hour. He chose to get up. Every evening another choice. Scroll for three hours. Or build for one. Neither choice changes your life in one day. But one of them made again and again does. Not every choice was right, his first company failed. He didn't call it the end, he called it a lesson. He adjusted and chose again. Day 1204, his first big client. When I looked back every scene was a choice. Each one pushed his life in a direction, some split apart, some came back together. All of them were connected, and everyone led to the same place. Then I was back, same field, same book. But now I knew how my story starts. So I turned to the first page and wrote it down. That's what Demure is for. You archive your dream today so you can see it tomorrow and break it down into small steps you can actually do.",
